// assembles them on the user's machine: the ones that are the game's own
// pickup voxels come out of their own game archives, Duke's come from
// Cheello's Voxel Duke 3D, and Domyoji's animation frames and edits are
// overlaid only when a VRaze install is supplied.

// Exhumed/PowerSlave VR weapon animation frame mappings
// Location: wadsrc/static/filter/exhumed/engine/vr_weapon_animations.def
//
// Maps specific game sequence tiles to alternate voxel tiles so the
// VR weapon model can change appearance mid-animation (e.g. open/closed
// bolt, raised/lowered weapon). Only needed for weapons that have
// visually distinct animation states worth representing in 3D.
//
// Format:
//   weapon <name>
//   {
//       frame <game_seq_tile>  <vr_tile>
//       ...
//   }
//
// The base tile (vr_tile = 30000 + weapon_slot*10) is always the default;
// entries here override it for specific sequence frames only.
//
// Exhumed sequences have not yet been mapped. Add entries here once
// voxel models are authored and specific frames are identified.
// See Blood's vr_weapon_animations.def (pitchfork, napalm) for examples.
